    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-transform-pattern:app:narrative:example-example-meta-transform-pattern-render" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-transform-pattern:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-transform-pattern:app:narrative:guide">
      <Body>Create a reusable pattern library and a separate workspace for concrete instances:

```text
meta-transform-pattern create --xml .\Patterns
meta-transform-pattern add-pattern --workspace .\Patterns --id insert-select --name "Insert select" &lt; insert-select.pattern.sql
meta-transform-pattern create-instance-workspace --xml .\PatternInstances
meta-transform-pattern add-instance --workspace .\PatternInstances --pattern-workspace .\Patterns --id load-customer --name LoadCustomer --pattern insert-select
```

Supply each placeholder through standard input, then materialize the instances:

```text
echo [dbo].[Customer] | meta-transform-pattern set-placeholder --workspace .\PatternInstances --pattern-workspace .\Patterns --instance load-customer --placeholder target
meta-convert transform-pattern-to-sql-script --pattern-workspace .\Patterns --instance-workspace .\PatternInstances --output-xml .\SqlScripts
```</Body>
      <LastReviewedImportBatchId></LastReviewedImportBatchId>
      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Example.example:meta-transform-pattern:render</Slot>
      <Title>Render pattern instances</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
    <DocumentationNarrative Id="source:cli:meta-transform-pattern:app:narrative:guide" DocumentationSubjectId="source:cli:meta-transform-pattern:app" PreviousNarrativeId="source:cli:meta-transform-pattern:app:narrative:summary">
      <Body>`MetaTransformPattern` and `MetaTransformPatternInstance` deliberately use separate workspaces. The pattern workspace is a reusable library of ordered SQL text and placeholders. The instance workspace identifies those patterns and supplies the concrete values used by one project.

`meta-transform-pattern` authors both workspace types. Definition commands use the pattern workspace; instance commands use the instance workspace together with `--pattern-workspace` so placeholder identities are resolved against the reusable definition. The sanctioned weave takes both workspaces and produces `MetaSqlScript`. SQL parsing remains in the existing MetaTransformScript importer.</Body>
      <LastReviewedImportBatchId></LastReviewedImportBatchId>
      <Origin>Authored</Origin>
      <ReviewStatus>Current</ReviewStatus>
      <Slot>Guide</Slot>
      <Title>Working with transform patterns</Title>
    </DocumentationNarrative>
